{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And if an altar of stones.</b> The altar that Moses built to cut a covenant with Israel with the blood of the covenant, and HaShem commanded that they build an altar of stones across the Jordan before they inherit the land, and write on the stones all the Torah, for many commandments depend on the land, just as there was need for their children when they entered the land because of the commandments that depend on the land, and there they sacrificed peace-offerings and ate as their ancestors did. And the meaning of \"and if an altar of stones\" is as if saying: make now an altar of earth, and if you merit to enter the land, then you shall build an altar of stones." "<b>Them.</b> They are the stones." "<b>Hewn.</b> The meaning is like \"and his minister Joshua son of Nun, a young man\" (Exodus 33:11) — thus: do not build them a hewn structure. And גזית is from the root of על גזזי צאנו (Genesis 38:12), כי גז חיש (Psalms 90:10), and likewise נגוזו ועבר (Nahum 1:12). And the meaning is like cutting — only whole stones, as they are created." "<b>For your sword.</b> The name חרב falls upon any iron tool made for cutting. Perhaps it is called thus because it destroys (מחרבת). And in another place it is written: \"You shall not wield iron upon them\" (Deuteronomy 27:5), concerning the altar of stones that they built. And it is not for us to seek the reasons of the commandments. And by way of reason, perhaps it was like the law of פגול — because [the tool] was brought near the altar, the remainder is not fit to be פגול, for \"he profanes the sacred thing he dedicated\" — there remains of it until it becomes פגול. And so too here: if they cut the stones to build the altar, perhaps what is cut off from the stones will be profaned for idolatry or for a defiled place, and this is not honor. And we have seen that the priest needs to atone for the altar."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {3 "The phrase 'ובמקום אחר' could refer either to Deuteronomy 27:5 cited immediately after or be an introductory remark; translated as a unit since the citation directly follows."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:37.353282785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}